  "statement": "Let $A$ be a local ring with maximal ideal $\\mathfrak m_A$ and let\n$O\\subseteq\\operatorname{Spec}(A)$ be open. Then the closed point\n$\\mathfrak m_A$ belongs to $O$ if and only if $O=\\operatorname{Spec}(A)$.",
  "proof": [
   {
    "text": "If $O=\\operatorname{Spec}(A)$, it contains $\\mathfrak m_A$. Conversely,\nchoose a basic open $D(a)$ with $\\mathfrak m_A\\in D(a)\\subseteq O$.\nThen $a\\notin\\mathfrak m_A$, hence $a$ is a unit of the local ring $A$ and\n$D(a)=\\operatorname{Spec}(A)$, so $O=\\operatorname{Spec}(A)$.",
    "uses": [],
    "elementary": null
   }
  ],
